      "side": 1,
      "message": "Partly fixed. The PS1 probe now prints `with-opt-feature` once `-I extra` is added and `without` once it\u0027s dropped, and so do a `cond-expand` in an included file and one nested in a `let`. But a `cond-expand` that reaches the body through a macro from another library still gets a stale entry:\n\n```scheme\n;; lib/shim.sld\n(define-library (shim)\n  (import (scheme base))\n  (export if-feature)\n  (begin\n    (define-syntax if-feature\n      (syntax-rules ()\n        ((_ yes no) (cond-expand ((library (opt feature)) yes) (else no)))))))\n;; lib/user.sld\n(define-library (user)\n  (import (scheme base) (shim))\n  (export which)\n  (begin (define which (if-feature \u0027with-opt-feature \u0027without))))\n;; main.scm\n(import (scheme base) (scheme write) (user))\n(display which) (newline)\n```\n\n- `vali --cache-dir C -I lib main.scm` prints `without` (cold).\n- `vali --cache-dir C -I lib -I extra main.scm`, where `extra/opt/feature.sld` exists, traces `loaded user.sld` and `stored shim.sld`, and prints `without`. `--no-cache` prints `with-opt-feature`.\n- The reverse also happens: a cache filled with `-I extra` keeps saying `with-opt-feature` after `extra` is dropped.\n\n`shim`\u0027s walk asks about `(opt feature)`, so its hash changes and it\u0027s recompiled. `user`\u0027s text has no `cond-expand`, so its hash is the same, and its `depends` check passes because `shim`\u0027s `library` and `syntax` sections didn\u0027t change. The answer `user` followed came from `cond_expand` (expand.rs:504), which reads the run-wide `available`.\n\nRecord in the artifact the answers that check gave while expanding the library and check them at load, or don\u0027t store a library whose expansion asked about a name its own walk didn\u0027t hash.",
      "parentUuid": "67e78ec3_86c6bf55",
      "revId": "b401f85c030810abf9c75a1534042d3d51ed55c7",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
