      "message": "This `?` makes a cache write fail the run, contrary to line 465 (\"what cannot be written is reported there, not raised\"). A library whose syntax export holds a datum label is enough:\n\n```scheme\n(define-syntax m (syntax-rules () ((_) \u0027(#1\u003d(x) #1#))))\n```\n\n- `--no-cache` prints `((x) (x))` and exits 0.\n- The default run prints `vali: encoding a syntax export: a datum label in a syntax export` and exits 1.\n- `vali build` fails the same way.\n\nPush the error to `report.failed` and continue, and add a test with such a library.",
